`index.md` is the artifact of both groom's and develop's `run` machine, so with no `--playbook` the
plan directory reports both playbooks, one YAML document each — develop's instance machine included,
its milestones found under the same directory.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan/index.md --
---
title: Plan
status: awaiting-approval
---
# Plan
-- fixtures/cwd/plan/milestones/M01-first/M01-first.md --
---
id: "01"
status: pending
---
# M01
-- cmd --
booping state plan/index.md
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
playbook: develop
workdir: {CWD}/plan
states:
  run:
    artifact: index.md
    status: awaiting-approval
    next:
    - to: ready-for-dev
      when: the user handed the plan to develop — invoking the run on it is the approval;
        intake takes this edge immediately, no confirmation asked
    - to: cancelled
      when: the user cancels the run
  milestone:
    artifact: milestones/{instance}/{instance}.md
    instances:
      M01-first:
        status: pending
        next:
        - to: in-progress
          when: the milestone's group is being handed to a worker
---
playbook: groom
workdir: {CWD}/plan
states:
  run:
    artifact: index.md
    status: awaiting-approval
    next:
    - to: drafting
      when: the user's change request touches the plan itself — architecture, scope,
        milestones, tasks or estimates
    - to: ready-for-dev
      when: the user explicitly approves the plan — "looks good" counts, silence never
        does
      gates:
      - explicit user approval captured
    - to: cancelled
      when: the user cancels the run
-- stderr --
